      "content": "You should structure your risk heat map around the core elements of social instability, which often correlate with specific demographic and environmental factors. Weighting historical crime data alongside population density is a solid start, but you must also incorporate indicators of social strain, such as unemployment rates and housing density within specific neighborhoods. Furthermore, including data on recent community complaints or social media sentiment, if available, can help predict where tensions are building before they become overt incidents.",
