      "content": "If the data consistently shows that specific demographic shifts correlate with higher incident rates, then the model is simply reflecting a documented pattern of behavior, which is what predictive analytics does. Focusing resources where the data indicates problems is efficient, but you must be aware that increased police presence in those areas will inevitably generate more recorded incidents, creating a feedback loop. This self-fulfilling prophecy is the inherent risk of using such models, regardless of the initial variables you choose.",
